  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "Bd5Rn12note1",
      "type": "note",
      "text": "**Background.** Paid UNATCO informant working the Battery Park / Hell's Kitchen beat in New York (2052). Feeds Manderley's people the word on NSF movements, arms shipments, and safe houses along the waterfront. Looks like a grey, paunchy dockside drunk \u2014 which is most of what he is now \u2014 but he still has sharper ears than most of the agents he reports to. Has a grown daughter he rarely talks about."
    },
    {
      "id": "2Z6gnote2",
      "type": "note",
      "text": "**How to play him.** Cynical, wry, talks out of the side of his mouth. Hits the bottle when nervous \u2014 which is often. Would rather talk his way out than draw the 9mm, but if he has to shoot he'll hit what he aims at \u2014 Guns (Pistol) 13, +1 initiative from Combat Reflexes, Fast-Draw (Pistol) 12. Lives in fear of being made as a rat."
    }
  ],
